(b2) residual floor vs stored decimal quantization
  magnitude min-decimals: median 15 (p05 14, p95 16)
  phase     min-decimals: median 14 (p05 13, p95 16)
  implied |dZ| half-step, worst case: median 2.617e-15  max 5.000e-07
  implied |dZ| half-step, uniform-rms: median 1.386e-15  max 2.887e-07
  observed residual floor (Lmax=14, rms over all cells): 5.926729e-07
  observed residual floor (L*= 9, max over energies): 8.089942e-06
  per-row: L=14 rms floor median 5.335e-07 vs per-row median stored half-step 2.449e-15
  ratio (per-row floor / per-row stored step), median over energies: 2.023e+08
  ratio (per-row floor / per-row stored step), max over energies: 7.005e+08
  -> the L=14 residual floor sits ABOVE the stored-value quantization, so a
     non-zero curvature survives even at L=14: the panel is not an exact
     finite-degree polynomial written down at the storage precision.
  CONTROL: re-store mag/phase at 5 significant digits (the experiment convention)
  and refit: L=4 rms floor 1.188519e-02 (stored panel 1.188512e-02) ; L=14 rms floor 2.026781e-05 (stored 5.926729e-07).
  -> at L=14 the 5-digit re-storage floor (2.027e-05) exceeds the stored panel floor
     (5.927e-07) by a factor 3.420e+01, confirming the stored theory values carry far more
     precision than the experiment convention.

